{
	"$description": "Hotstring action entries (_shared/hotstrings/engine/matcher/action_entry.lua): `fields` are the action fields a parsed entry carries or the refusal that skips it; `plans` the edit before the action, with the trigger erased (default) or kept as typed, end character included (« effacer le déclencheur » off); `saves` are editor saves through the personal-file model (what the written entry contains, lacks, or why the save is refused); `matches` replay a TOML line through the shared reader and matcher (the event on screen, as on Linux and Windows). Replayed by the macOS and Linux suites (_shared/tests/lua/hotstrings/action_entry_contract.lua) and the AutoHotkey port. null means the key is absent.",
	"fields": [
		{
			"id": "text_entry",
			"entry": {
				"output": "x"
			},
			"fields": null
		},
		{
